From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-24)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: share the port's non-Apple code paths

The sweet port's guards mean "this is the Qualcomm phone port, not Apple
silicon": no corecrypto kext, no AppleImage4/AMFI, no monitor, no closed
per-SoC assembly. MILANF needs every one of them, and MILANF's own DTB
confirms the topology assumptions behind two of them: all eight CPUs carry
enable-method = psci and reg = 0x0/0x100/.../0x700, so the core id really is
in MPIDR Aff1 (same as SM7150) and the PSCI CPU_ON entry is required.

Widened: start.s (MPIDR core decode, sweet_secondary_entry, local TLB/I
invalidation before MMU), cpu.c (bootstrap-structure PoC clean, bring-up
observer), machine_routines.c (cpus=N default + clamp, Aff1 cluster decode,
ml_enable_monitor stub), vm_kern.c (per-CPU kmem RNG without corecrypto),
entropy.c and prng_random.c (built-in HMAC-SHA256 DRBG instead of the absent
corecrypto kext), kern_trustcache.c (no Image4/AMFI runtime).

Not touched here: the framebuffer and early-console sites in start.s,
arm_vm_init.c, sweet_early.[ch] and debug.c, and the iokit/Kernel/arm drivers.
Those carry sweet's framebuffer base and geometry and need per-machine
values plus an L3 mapping (0x85200000 is only 2MB-aligned, so sweet's single
32MB L2 block cannot cover milanf's carveout).

